    <string name="settings_export_format">Default export format</string>
    <string name="settings_about">About</string>
    <string name="settings_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="settings_about_body">Every value in this app is read from an Android API on this device. Nothing is inferred, benchmarked or estimated. Where the platform will not answer, the row says which API was called and why.\n\nThe app works entirely offline. It holds no INTERNET permission, has no account, no analytics and no server, so nothing it reads can leave the device except through an export you share yourself.</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_title">What this app does not read</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body">Biometric templates and hardware-backed key material are non-exportable by Android’s hardware design; this app reports only classification — whether the sensor exists, whether the keystore is hardware-backed, which biometric strength class is available. Stable device identifiers such as the hardware serial and the DRM device unique ID are readable but deliberately not read, and those rows say so.</string>

